  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Some Spanish verbs change their stem vowel in stressed present‑tense forms: o→ue (poder→puedo), e→ie (querer→quiero), and e→i (seguir→sigo). These changes occur in all singular forms and in the third person plural, but not in the first person plural."
